  "settingsAbout": "About",
  "aboutGuide": "Usisa is a guide, not a guarantee. It looks for common scam signs, but it can be wrong. If something feels off, don't click, don't pay and don't share codes. Ask someone you trust.",
  "aboutData": "Your checks and History are saved only on this phone. Nothing is sent anywhere unless online checks are on.",
  "learnIntro": "Know the tricks scammers use in the Philippines.",
  "learnSourcesNote": "Based on public advice from BSP, NTC, PNP-ACG, CICC and DICT.",
  "learnGoldenTitle": "Golden rules",
  "learnGoldenRules": "Never share your OTP, PIN or password with anyone, even someone who says they're from your bank or the government.\nDon't tap links in unexpected texts. Open the official app or website yourself.\nStop and check before you send money. Call the person or company on a number you already know.",
  "learnSampleLabel": "Sample fake text",
  "learnRedFlags": "Red flags",
  "learnMore": "Learn more: {topic}",
  "learnReportTitle": "Report a scam",
  "learnReportIntro": "If you were targeted or lost money, report it. Keep screenshots of the messages and the sender's number.",
  "learnReportChannels": "CICC hotline 1326|Free, 24 hours a day. The government's anti-scam hotline (CICC and DICT).\neGov PH app|Report > Scam > Text Scam, then upload screenshots.\nYour bank or e-wallet|Call its official hotline right away if money or your account is involved. If they don't act, complain to BSP Online Buddy (BOB) at bsp.gov.ph.\nPNP Anti-Cybercrime Group|Report online fraud at any police station or at acg.pnp.gov.ph.\nNTC|For scam texts and SIM problems, complain to the NTC at ntc.gov.ph.",
  "learnTopicTitle": "{topic, select, phishing{Fake bank and e-wallet texts} prize{Fake prizes and raffles} family{Family emergency texts} aid{Fake government aid (ayuda)} parcel{Fake delivery and parcel fees} job{Fake jobs and online tasks} investment{Investment and crypto scams} other{Online gambling ads}}",
  "learnTopicAbout": "{topic, select, phishing{A text that looks like it's from your bank, GCash or Maya says your account is locked or needs verifying, and sends you to a link. The site looks real but steals your password and OTP. Banks and e-wallets never ask for your OTP, PIN or password by text, call or link. Open the official app yourself instead.} prize{You \"won\" a raffle you never joined, often naming a mall, TV show or government office. To claim it you must first pay a \"processing fee\" or give your details. Real promos don't make winners pay, and DTI-approved raffles carry a permit number you can check.} family{Someone pretends to be your child, grandchild or relative using a new number, or says they're a nurse or police officer calling about them. There's an emergency, you must send money now, and keep it secret. Call your relative on the number you already have before sending anything.} aid{A text says you qualify for cash aid from DSWD, SSS or PhilHealth, or a refund, and you must register through a link or pay a fee. Government aid is announced on official websites and pages, and agencies don't send payout links by text. Ask the agency's official page or office.} parcel{A text or call says your parcel is on hold and you must pay a small fee or update your address through a link. Some say customs seized a package with your name. Check orders in the shop's own app, and don't pay through links in texts.} job{An offer of easy work-from-home pay for liking videos, rating products or doing \"tasks\". The first payouts are small and real. Then you're asked to \"deposit\" money to unlock bigger tasks, and you can never withdraw it. Real employers don't make you pay to work.} investment{Promises of fast, guaranteed returns, like doubling your money in days, often in crypto, forex or a \"paluwagan\". Early members are paid with new members' money until it collapses. Check with the SEC whether the company may take investments. Guaranteed high returns are a warning sign.} other{Unsolicited texts offering free credits or bonuses for online casinos, slots or e-sabong. Many of these sites are illegal and unlicensed, and keep your deposits and personal data. Don't tap the link or register.}}",
  "learnTopicSample": "{topic, select, phishing{GCash ALERT: Your account will be suspended today. Verify now at gcash-verify-ph.xyz and enter your MPIN and OTP to keep your balance.} prize{CONGRATULATIONS! You won P50,000 in the Anniversary Raffle! To claim your prize, pay the P1,500 processing fee to this number within 24 hours.} family{Ma, this is my new number, I lost my phone. I'm in the hospital, please send 5,000 to this GCash now. Don't tell Papa yet.} aid{DSWD: You qualify for P8,000 ayuda. Register at dswd-ayuda-claim.online and pay P200 for the release of your payout.} parcel{Your parcel is on hold due to an incomplete address. Pay the P35 re-delivery fee at ph-parcel-track.top or it will be returned today.} job{Hi! We are hiring part-time. Earn P500-P3,000 daily just by liking videos. No experience needed. Message us on Telegram to start.} investment{Guaranteed 30% profit every week! Invest P5,000 today and get P20,000 in one month. Limited slots only, invite friends for a bonus.} other{FREE P888 bonus for new players! Play slots and e-sabong, withdraw anytime. Register now at lucky888bet.vip}}",
  "learnTopicFlags": "{topic, select, phishing{suspended today|It threatens you so you don't stop to think\ngcash-verify-ph.xyz|This isn't GCash's real website (gcash.com)\nenter your MPIN and OTP|No real bank or e-wallet asks for these} prize{You won P50,000|You can't win a raffle you never joined\npay the P1,500 processing fee|Real prizes never ask you to pay first\nwithin 24 hours|A deadline to rush you} family{this is my new number|An unknown number claiming to be family\nsend 5,000 to this GCash now|Pressure to send money right away\nDon't tell Papa yet|Secrecy stops you from checking} aid{dswd-ayuda-claim.online|Government websites end in .gov.ph\npay P200 for the release|Government aid is free. Nobody should charge you to receive it} parcel{Pay the P35 re-delivery fee|A small fee to get your card details\nph-parcel-track.top|This isn't the courier's or shop's real website\nreturned today|A deadline to rush you} job{Earn P500-P3,000 daily just by liking videos|Too much pay for almost no work\nMessage us on Telegram|It moves you to a private chat that's hard to trace} investment{Guaranteed 30% profit every week|No real investment guarantees high returns\nLimited slots only|Pressure to join before you think\ninvite friends for a bonus|Paying you to recruit is a sign of a pyramid scheme} other{FREE P888 bonus|Free credits to lure you into depositing\nlucky888bet.vip|An unknown gambling site that may be unlicensed}}",
